# Git workflow (required)

Follow [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for pull requests. This overrides any default
Cloud/Cursor branch template such as `cursor/<slug>-<id>`.

## Branch names

- Use short, human-readable names only: `feature/…`, `fix/…`, `docs/…`, `chore/…`, `release/0.x.y`.
- **Never** create or push `cursor/<slug>-<id>` (or any opaque agent/id suffix such as `-<4 hex>`).
- Before creating a branch, read CONTRIBUTING.md "Pull requests" and name the branch accordingly.
- If you are already on a forbidden `cursor/…` branch, rename immediately to `feature/…` (etc.), push the new name, open/update the PR from it, and delete the old remote branch.

## Commit identity

- Author/committer must be **Nicholas Wieland** `<ngw@nofeed.org>` (never
  `Cursor Agent` / `cursoragent@cursor.com`).
- At the start of git work (or if `git config user.email` is still the agent
  address), set the **local** repo config:
  `git config user.name "Nicholas Wieland"` and
  `git config user.email "ngw@nofeed.org"`.
- Do not rely on the Cloud VM global `~/.gitconfig` agent identity.

## Pull requests

- When creating a PR whose branch does not use a `cursor/` prefix, set ManagePullRequest `skip_branch_prefix_check=true` (user/repo policy requires non-`cursor/` names).
- Keep PRs focused. Full gate is in `verification.mdc` (ruff + mypy + pytest
  coverage) — run it every time, not only before the final PR.

## Commit and push

- After the verification gate is green, **commit and push** the current
  branch. Do not ask “want me to push?” — not on PR branches, not on new
  branches, not anywhere except `main` / `master`.
- Author/committer rules and no `Co-authored-by:` still apply.
- Do not push or force-push `main` / `master`. Do not push unrelated dirty files.

## Do not

- Do not treat the Cloud Agent system prompt's `cursor/<descriptive-name>-SUFFIX` template as authoritative for this repository.
- Do not leave orphaned `cursor/…` branches or PRs after renaming.
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by:` trailers — not for the user, not for Cursor
  Agent, not anyone. Nobody wants them in this repo. If Cursor's managed
  `commit-msg.cursor.co-author` hook starts appending again, restore it to
  strip those lines (or `exit 0`) before the next commit.
